-Adjudications carried here as bytes rather than left on ed3c/skill-concerns#59
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+Adjudications carried as bytes (ed3c/skill-concerns#59) - AGENTS.md is the source
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
-Runtime/ceremony boundary: a supervising reader owns RUNTIME liveness of the
-sessions it watches; CEREMONY correctness (receipt verbatim discipline, marker
-transitions, handoff) stays with the skill that owns that ceremony. One skill,
-one concern; a restated copy is the drift the split exists to prevent.
-
-Filing-not-reflex coupling: an observation-time finding never auto-invokes this
-pass. Findings are FILED at a strict destination with an owner, and the daily
-cadence consumes them on its own schedule. An auto-maintain path would let a
-reader rewrite its own lens until a finding disappears - self-laundering, the
-write path the reader-only contract forbids.
-
-Trigger-not-apply exception: when a driver's own selftest goes red mid-
-observation, the observation report auto-degrades to lens-suspect and one
-maintain pass is SCHEDULED. Trigger automation keeps every gate; application
-automation removes them, and only the first is admitted.
+The runtime/ceremony boundary, filing-not-reflex coupling, and trigger-not-
+apply exception rulings live in AGENTS.md ("Adjudications carried here as
+bytes"), not here. AGENTS.md's own rule for this kind of split is "POINT at
+it, never restate it; a restated copy is the drift the split exists to
+prevent" - this module obeys that rule about itself: this pass's behavior
+(no auto-invoke, no auto-apply, filed findings) is the enforcement of those
+three rulings, not a second copy of their prose.
+tests/test_maintain_skills.py::test_maintain_docs_carry_the_sc59_adjudications
+is the mechanical reader, and it reads AGENTS.md.
 
